        "body": "Submitting another issue for #1268, because I can't reopen it. I believe the issue was not solved.\nA help for a subcommand subc2 is not shown if subc1 has a positional option and is not provided for the help message.\n\nBelow is the minimum reproducible example.\nAs you can see, .calling `/cli11_help_bug subc1 subc2 --help` provides help on subc1, not subc2.\n\n```shell\n$> ./cli11_help_bug subc1 --help\nFirst subcommand\n\n\n./cli11_help_bug subc1 [OPTIONS] ID [SUBCOMMAND]\n\n\nPOSITIONALS:\n  ID INT REQUIRED             Object ID\n\nOPTIONS:\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\n\nSUBCOMMANDS:\n  subc2                       Nested subcommand\n$> ./cli11_help_bug subc1 subc2 --help\nFirst subcommand\n\n\n./cli11_help_bug subc1 [OPTIONS] ID [SUBCOMMAND]\n\n\nPOSITIONALS:\n  ID INT REQUIRED             Object ID\n\nOPTIONS:\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\n\nSUBCOMMANDS:\n  subc2                       Nested subcommand\n```\n\n### Reproduction example\n\n```c++\n#include <CLI/CLI.hpp>\n\nint main(int argc, char** argv) {\n    CLI::App app{\"CLI11 help bug MRE\"};\n\n    auto* subc1 = app.add_subcommand(\"subc1\", \"First subcommand\");\n\n    int id{};\n    subc1->add_option(\"ID\", id, \"Object ID\")->required();\n\n    auto* subc2 = subc1->add_subcommand(\"subc2\", \"Nested subcommand\");\n\n    bool flag{false};\n    subc2->add_flag(\"--flag\", flag, \"Example flag\");\n\n    CLI11_PARSE(app, argc, argv);\n\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n\nAdding positional argument:\n```\n$ ./cli11_help_bug subc1 1 subc2 --help\nNested subcommand\n\n\n./cli11_help_bug subc1 subc2 [OPTIONS]\n\n\nOPTIONS:\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\n          --flag              Example flag\n```",
